invariant: INV-16
file: ct.h
catches: test/widemul-builds.sh
reason: ct.h takes the X25519=wide field in a host object, so an object built
  outside the Makefile runs the 64x64->128 multiply its build stated for
  every session, whatever each session's ch_cfg.cpu states.
  test/widemul-builds.sh requires that build not to compile.

--- old
#ifdef CH_CPU_RUNTIME
#error "X25519=wide states its multiply's timing at build time; a host object asks each session"
#endif
--- new
